   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I do not know yet whether I can parse the model specified in <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">SimMatrix</font> to lavaan.</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Not anymore.  Back in 2011/2012, simsem used to write lavaan syntax as I suggested you do.  Subsequently, it changed to writing parameter tables (see <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">?model.syntax</font> and <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">?parTable</font>), which I think turned out to be a mistake.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423907356000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ONjIqTfmlEMkfo8laG-vq\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div></div>"
